WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.984 --> 00:00:05.975
Check the film on that kid.

2
00:00:08.745 --> 00:00:10.337
AL: <i>Take a deep breath.</i>

3
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:12.575
Inhale. exhale. Again.

4
00:00:12.825 --> 00:00:13.895
Slowly.

5
00:00:15.626 --> 00:00:18.186
RICHARD: [Whispers] Check the film.

6
00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:20.258
AL: <i>Take it easy.</i>

7
00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:25.460
What's the status on that kid?

8
00:00:25.547 --> 00:00:26.981
AL: Possible fractured sternum.

9
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.218
ANNE: Get over here. I need you.

10
00:00:29.308 --> 00:00:32.744
Can you help us?
Bring this kid to Observation Room Two.

11
00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:36.218
Yeah. you. Come on. help us out. okay?

12
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.029
How are you. champ?

13
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:47.465
My chest hurts.

14
00:00:48.511 --> 00:00:50.183
Does it hurt when you breathe?

15
00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:51.420
BO Y: <i>Yes.</i>

16
00:00:55.712 --> 00:00:58.385
RICHARD: What's your name?
JOEL: Joel.

17
00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:04.587
Look at this.

18
00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:07.633
SAM: <i>We're eating oranges</i>
<i>and we're making IDs.</i>

19
00:01:07.714 --> 00:01:10.023
"C.C.H." What the hell is that?

20
00:01:10.114 --> 00:01:11.945
Cook County Hospital.

21
00:01:15.155 --> 00:01:17.350
RICHARD: <i>Just hang on. okay?</i>

22
00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:19.468
You'll be okay. pal.

23
00:01:19.636 --> 00:01:20.705
You'll be just fine.

24
00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:22.434
Hold that elevator.

25
00:01:23.156 --> 00:01:24.191
Thank you.

26
00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:29.391
RICHARD: <i>How're you doing?</i>

27
00:01:29.477 --> 00:01:30.956
My chest hurts.

28
00:01:31.877 --> 00:01:33.231
Where's your mom. pal?

29
00:01:33.318 --> 00:01:34.433
I don't know.

30
00:01:34.518 --> 00:01:36.349
Is she at home?

31
00:01:36.518 --> 00:01:38.429
I think she's with my brother.

32
00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.191
Your brother? They're downstairs?

33
00:01:40.279 --> 00:01:41.951
JOEL: <i>I don't know.</i>

34
00:01:42.039 --> 00:01:43.358
Don't worry.

35
00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:45.312
We'll find her for you.

36
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.919
RICHARD: <i>What are you?</i>
<i>Football player? Baseball player?</i>

37
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.479
JOEL: Football.

38
00:01:51.961 --> 00:01:53.235
Hold on. son.

39
00:02:04.602 --> 00:02:05.797
Hey. Doctor.

40
00:02:06.603 --> 00:02:08.912
They sent this one from downstairs.

41
00:02:14.844 --> 00:02:17.836
Get this one into Room Four. stat.

42
00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.716
RICHARD: <i>Bye-bye. Joel.</i>

43
00:02:33.087 --> 00:02:35.078
Where's that boy I sent here?

44
00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.759
GLADYS: What boy?
ANNE: The one with the fractured sternum.

45
00:02:36.847 --> 00:02:38.964
He never came through here.

46
00:02:39.808 --> 00:02:40.843
He didn't?

47
00:02:40.928 --> 00:02:42.361
No. he didn't.

48
00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:48.686
Do you have a particular interest
in our patient's X-rays?

49
00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:50.361
What do you mean?

50
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.808
I saw you looking at that boy's chest film.

51
00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.199
- It's a hobby of mine.
- It's a hobby. really?

52
00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.600
What's your other hobby. brain surgery?

53
00:02:58.691 --> 00:02:59.885
What do you want?

54
00:02:59.971 --> 00:03:01.165
To know how that boy got to surgery.

55
00:03:01.251 --> 00:03:03.401
I'm a janitor. I do as I'm told.

56
00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:04.527
That's bullshit!

57
00:03:04.612 --> 00:03:06.648
Who changed those orders?

58
00:03:07.092 --> 00:03:09.208
I don't know what you mean.

59
00:03:12.093 --> 00:03:13.890
You stay right there.

60
00:03:15.573 --> 00:03:17.326
ANNE: Call Security!

61
00:03:20.694 --> 00:03:22.252
ANNE: Hey! Hey!

62
00:03:24.855 --> 00:03:26.573
RICHARD: Excuse me.

63
00:03:28.095 --> 00:03:29.574
[Tires screech]

64
00:03:31.536 --> 00:03:32.730
[Siren wails]

65
00:03:43.578 --> 00:03:47.332
Tell Stevens to get hold of
that guy Kelly over at C.P.D.

66
00:03:49.499 --> 00:03:53.936
A guy disguised as a janitor orders
an emergency medical procedure...

67
00:03:54.139 --> 00:03:57.337
...and all you did was
take away his I.D. Card?

68
00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.494
No. I called Security. He took off down
the hall. What was I supposed to do?

69
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:02.980
Listen. Mr...

70
00:04:03.101 --> 00:04:04.375
SAM: <i>Deputy.</i>

71
00:04:04.461 --> 00:04:05.530
Gerard.

72
00:04:07.181 --> 00:04:08.534
I'm really tired.

73
00:04:08.621 --> 00:04:10.533
I'd like to go home now.

74
00:04:10.622 --> 00:04:12.135
Okay. How's the boy doing?

75
00:04:12.222 --> 00:04:13.860
He saved his life.

76
00:04:18.703 --> 00:04:19.931
Thank you.

77
00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.261
"Desmondo. José Ruiz."

78
00:04:31.585 --> 00:04:32.938
Where're you at. Desmondo?

79
00:04:34.945 --> 00:04:37.221
Okay. Sam. this is my problem.

80
00:04:37.666 --> 00:04:40.385
The place is crawling with cops. right?

81
00:04:40.466 --> 00:04:42.697
Everybody's looking
for Richard Kimble. right?

82
00:04:42.787 --> 00:04:44.778
So why would a guy be stupid enough...

83
00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:46.937
...to hang out in the trauma ward
and play Mother Teresa?

84
00:04:47.027 --> 00:04:48.256
Excuse me.

85
00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:07.462
You. guys. have a problem?

86
00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.461
No.

87
00:05:08.711 --> 00:05:10.827
No. no. No problem at all.

88
00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:20.587
SAM: Excuse me. could we
have a word with you. please?

89
00:05:22.153 --> 00:05:25.111
This is Dr. Elway at Cook County Hospital.

90
00:05:27.153 --> 00:05:31.147
I'm following-up for the prosthetic clinic
on Matthew Zelick.

91
00:05:33.074 --> 00:05:34.349
Oh. he did?

92
00:05:34.515 --> 00:05:36.233
I'm terribly sorry.

93
00:05:39.315 --> 00:05:40.749
Right or left?

94
00:05:41.236 --> 00:05:42.271
Right.

95
00:05:43.916 --> 00:05:45.952
SAM: Age?
POOLE: <i>35 to 45.</i>

96
00:05:46.837 --> 00:05:50.432
This is Ted Riley
with the High School Reunion Committee.

97
00:05:50.517 --> 00:05:53.270
25 years are right around the corner...

98
00:05:53.358 --> 00:05:56.634
...and Clive is on our list
of missing in action.

99
00:05:57.038 --> 00:06:00.793
The information gave me a number.
but when I tried it...

100
00:06:02.079 --> 00:06:03.353
No kidding.

101
00:06:05.999 --> 00:06:07.433
Armed robbery?

102
00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.428
He's where?

103
00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.555
Point of attachments?

104
00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.675
Mid-humerus.

105
00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.877
That gives us 47 possibles.

106
00:06:15.161 --> 00:06:16.037
47?

107
00:06:16.681 --> 00:06:19.320
Robert. cross-check these people
for criminal records.

108
00:06:19.401 --> 00:06:20.437
BIGGS: Wait a minute.

109
00:06:21.482 --> 00:06:23.234
[Motor boat revving]

110
00:06:25.082 --> 00:06:27.802
[Bagpipes blare. marching drum plays]

111
00:06:31.163 --> 00:06:34.520
MEGAPHONE: <i>Happy St. Patrick's Day</i>
<i>to all of you.</i>

112
00:06:58.688 --> 00:07:00.485
[Elevator bell rings]

113
00:07:11.249 --> 00:07:13.718
COP: Hey there. what's happening?

114
00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.368
BIGGS: Driscoll. Clive R.

115
00:07:19.451 --> 00:07:22.807
BIGGS: One-armed man. armed robbery.
That's funny.

116
00:07:23.611 --> 00:07:25.170
BIGGS: Question:

117
00:07:29.292 --> 00:07:31.409
BIGGS: If they can dye
this river green today...

118
00:07:31.493 --> 00:07:34.565
...why can't they dye
it blue the other days?

119
00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:36.450
Biggs. how do I know?

120
00:07:38.054 --> 00:07:40.852
HENRY: So. what are you Irish. sir?
SAM: Who. me? No.

121
00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:42.287
SAM: Are you?

122
00:07:42.374 --> 00:07:43.853
HENRY: No. man!

123
00:07:53.576 --> 00:07:54.804
Name of inmate?

124
00:07:55.136 --> 00:07:56.410
Clive Driscoll.

125
00:07:56.736 --> 00:07:58.056
Driscoll. Clive.

126
00:07:58.377 --> 00:07:59.730
I.D.. please.

127
00:07:59.977 --> 00:08:01.729
<i>Driscoll. Clive R.</i>

128
00:08:01.897 --> 00:08:03.330
<i>2- 0-1-0.</i>

129
00:08:03.577 --> 00:08:07.776
Be advised that under federal court ruling.
your conversation can be recorded.

130
00:08:08.058 --> 00:08:09.127
<i>Sign here. please!</i>

131
00:08:09.218 --> 00:08:13.656
This is hinky. He is a college graduate.
He wouldn't go through all this security...

132
00:08:13.739 --> 00:08:17.892
...go to the county lock-up to find
someone his own people say doesn't exist.

133
00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:18.970
Hinky.

134
00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.539
What does that mean. "hinky"?

135
00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:21.769
BIGGS: Strange.
HENRY: Weird.

136
00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.329
Say "strange" or "weird."
"Hinky" has no meaning.

137
00:08:24.421 --> 00:08:25.854
Why not say "hinky"?

138
00:08:27.621 --> 00:08:31.615
I don't want you using meaningless words
around me. I'm taking the stairs.

139
00:08:31.982 --> 00:08:33.540
How about "bullshit"?

140
00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.980
Visitor for Driscoll.

141
00:08:40.303 --> 00:08:42.498
Come on. let's go. let's go.

142
00:08:45.704 --> 00:08:47.342
GUARD: <i>Over there.</i>

143
00:08:59.826 --> 00:09:01.384
[Exhales deeply]

144
00:09:03.027 --> 00:09:05.746
[Woman and inmate speaking in Spanish]

145
00:09:09.228 --> 00:09:11.298
GUARD: <i>Let's go. Driscoll.</i>

146
00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:18.944
GUARD: You've got five minutes.

147
00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:20.826
Who the hell are you?

148
00:09:20.949 --> 00:09:23.418
Look. I'm sorry. I made a mistake.

149
00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:25.148
CLIVE: You got me down here...

150
00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.822
...might as well talk.

151
00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:30.586
Down here you got no entertainment.
Ain't no cable here.

152
00:09:31.951 --> 00:09:35.182
Listen. pal. I wish I could. but I can't.
Sorry.

153
00:10:22.879 --> 00:10:23.834
Richard!

154
00:11:25.808 --> 00:11:29.484
Officer. there is a man in a blue coat
waving a gun and screaming... at a woman.

155
00:11:29.569 --> 00:11:30.763
SAM: Stop that man!

156
00:11:30.849 --> 00:11:32.407
HENRY: He's a U.S. Marshal! Let him go!

157
00:11:32.489 --> 00:11:34.128
HENRY: Let him go!

158
00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.967
SAM: Close the gates!

159
00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.730
[Woman screams]

160
00:11:44.331 --> 00:11:46.368
[Buzzer ringing at gates]

161
00:11:52.613 --> 00:11:53.728
SAM: Hold it!

162
00:11:53.813 --> 00:11:55.769
[Loud multiple gunshots]

163
00:11:55.853 --> 00:11:57.491
[People screaming]

164
00:12:10.735 --> 00:12:12.488
SAM: Open the doors!

165
00:12:20.737 --> 00:12:22.170
We're on the roof.

166
00:12:22.257 --> 00:12:23.610
We're on the roof.

167
00:12:23.857 --> 00:12:26.656
BIGGS: Take some men! Look down there!

168
00:12:27.138 --> 00:12:28.571
Jesus. he's in the plaza. Sam!

169
00:12:28.658 --> 00:12:30.091
He's heading east!

170
00:12:32.259 --> 00:12:35.217
BIGGS: <i>He's going east</i>
<i>toward the Picasso!</i>

171
00:12:37.579 --> 00:12:39.218
[Wings fluttering]

172
00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.534
[Marching band. bagpipes playing]

173
00:12:44.821 --> 00:12:48.860
[Announcements over megaphone.
whistles blowing. crowd noise]

174
00:13:05.504 --> 00:13:07.142
[Cymbals crashing]

175
00:13:23.706 --> 00:13:25.425
[Bagpipes blaring]

176
00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:51.467
MEGAPHONE: <i>Happy St. Patrick's Day</i>
<i>to all of you.</i>

177
00:13:54.391 --> 00:13:57.350
[Snare drums building.
playing loud march]

178
00:14:05.673 --> 00:14:07.311
[Whistles blowing]

179
00:14:14.994 --> 00:14:19.625
Deputy Gerard. why do you feel
that Dr. Kimble came back to Chicago?

180
00:14:20.115 --> 00:14:21.389
I have no idea.

181
00:14:21.555 --> 00:14:24.275
We understand your deputies
were at the hospital today.

182
00:14:24.356 --> 00:14:26.187
Was Dr. Kimble at the hospital?

183
00:14:26.276 --> 00:14:28.346
I don't have any comment on that one.

184
00:14:28.436 --> 00:14:30.428
Let me get the chronology straight.

185
00:14:30.517 --> 00:14:33.236
The subject was tried.
convicted. incarcerated...

186
00:14:33.437 --> 00:14:38.034
...escaped. presumed dead. and is now
at large in Chicago. Is that correct. sir?

187
00:14:38.118 --> 00:14:40.268
Except for being presumed dead.

188
00:14:40.358 --> 00:14:43.237
Do you believe that Kimble's
armed and dangerous?

189
00:14:43.439 --> 00:14:45.395
KELLY: I believe he's dangerous. yes.

190
00:14:45.479 --> 00:14:49.553
He's taking chances. coming back. Do you
feel that perhaps he might be innocent?

191
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:53.872
No. he's not innocent. He was convicted
in a court of law. He's guilty.

192
00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.111
REPORTER: How will you try to catch him?

193
00:14:56.201 --> 00:14:59.113
SAM: We have no further comments
for now.

194
00:15:16.564 --> 00:15:18.316
[Propellers pelting]

195
00:15:22.485 --> 00:15:25.318
[Blues music playing. ambient bar noise]

196
00:15:32.326 --> 00:15:33.805
[Phone ringing]

197
00:16:40.137 --> 00:16:42.173
[Dog barking in distance]

198
00:16:46.738 --> 00:16:48.330
[Shattering]

199
00:17:09.541 --> 00:17:11.577
[Dog howling in distance]

200
00:18:31.754 --> 00:18:33.551
[Dance music playing]

201
00:18:34.634 --> 00:18:35.749
<i>Alec.</i>

202
00:18:35.994 --> 00:18:37.269
<i>Richard Kimble.</i>

203
00:18:39.035 --> 00:18:41.913
RICHARD: Hi. how are you.
ALEC: Good. Dr. Kimble.

204
00:18:41.995 --> 00:18:43.030
Lentz!

205
00:18:43.755 --> 00:18:47.829
ALEC: <i>Sorry. we've been trading phone</i>
<i>calls the last few days.</i>

206
00:19:06.959 --> 00:19:09.837
MAN: <i>A cruise sponsored by</i>
<i>Devlin MacGregor...</i>

207
00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.717
<i>... that could be fun.</i>

208
00:19:17.201 --> 00:19:19.396
- <i>Cancún. Richard.</i>
- <i>Sport fishing.</i>

209
00:19:19.481 --> 00:19:20.880
<i>Piña coladas.</i>

210
00:19:20.961 --> 00:19:23.112
What must the hospital buy?
What's the catch?

211
00:19:23.202 --> 00:19:24.237
Sailfish.

212
00:19:24.802 --> 00:19:26.838
No. there are no strings attached.

213
00:19:27.242 --> 00:19:30.076
<i>So what do you say? So what do you say?</i>

214
00:19:32.003 --> 00:19:35.040
RICHARD: This guy is bleeding from
every needle puncture.

215
00:19:35.123 --> 00:19:38.400
STEVENS: Lentz sent this guy in?
Is he on that wonder drug?

216
00:19:38.484 --> 00:19:41.476
Yes. he's on the RDU-90 protocol. Provasic.

217
00:19:41.924 --> 00:19:43.244
RICHARD: Drug of the future. boys.

218
00:19:43.325 --> 00:19:47.318
RICHARD: Clean out those arteries
and put us out of business.

219
00:19:51.686 --> 00:19:54.883
"Parade Master of Ceremonies
Ed O'Flaherty said...

220
00:19:55.046 --> 00:19:58.801
"...he didn't recall a livelier parade
during the last 20 years.

221
00:19:58.887 --> 00:20:00.161
BIGGS: <i>"That Kimble...</i>

222
00:20:00.247 --> 00:20:02.318
"...is some kind of lad..."

223
00:20:02.648 --> 00:20:04.559
SAM: "Lad?"
BIGGS: Yeah. "lad."

224
00:20:06.888 --> 00:20:09.403
BIGGS: Maybe he's a leprechaun.
I'm quoting this guy.

225
00:20:09.489 --> 00:20:12.003
Some guy on line three claims
he's Richard Kimble.

226
00:20:12.089 --> 00:20:13.124
BIGGS: Who is it?

227
00:20:13.209 --> 00:20:14.244
COSMO: We got another Kimble
on line three.

228
00:20:14.329 --> 00:20:15.683
Henry. let me see that phone.

229
00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:17.169
BIGGS: <i>Tell him he looks good in a beard.</i>

230
00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.649
NEWMAN: What line?
SECRETARY: <i>Three.</i>

231
00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:22.326
BIGGS: <i>"I hope he was able to wear</i>
<i>a little green. sip some whiskey..."</i>

232
00:20:22.411 --> 00:20:24.527
[Chuckling] This is Gerard.

233
00:20:25.051 --> 00:20:28.168
Do you remember what I told you
in the tunnel?

234
00:20:29.332 --> 00:20:30.890
POOLE: <i>It's him!</i>

235
00:20:30.972 --> 00:20:33.202
SAM: I remember it was noisy.

236
00:20:33.292 --> 00:20:35.682
Well. I think you said something like...

237
00:20:35.773 --> 00:20:37.525
...you didn't kill your wife.

238
00:20:37.613 --> 00:20:39.285
Remember what you told me?

239
00:20:39.853 --> 00:20:42.288
I remember you were pointing
my gun at me.

240
00:20:45.694 --> 00:20:48.163
You said. "I don't care."

241
00:20:48.415 --> 00:20:50.565
[Whispering] He's on the south side.

242
00:20:50.655 --> 00:20:53.123
Yeah. Richard. that's right. I don't care.

243
00:20:53.215 --> 00:20:55.525
I'm not trying to solve a puzzle. here.

244
00:20:55.616 --> 00:20:57.607
Well. I am trying to solve a puzzle.

245
00:20:57.696 --> 00:20:59.254
Five seconds to location.

246
00:20:59.336 --> 00:21:01.567
And I just found a big piece.

247
00:21:01.657 --> 00:21:02.931
Richard...

248
00:21:04.417 --> 00:21:05.532
Richard?

249
00:21:06.297 --> 00:21:08.209
SAM: <i>Richard? Richard?</i>

250
00:21:10.418 --> 00:21:11.612
SAM: <i>Hello. Richard?</i>

251
00:21:11.698 --> 00:21:13.893
He didn't hang up the phone.

252
00:21:14.259 --> 00:21:15.374
Where is he?

253
00:21:15.459 --> 00:21:16.733
256 South St. Lawrence.

254
00:21:16.819 --> 00:21:19.049
Get the C.P.D. Right the hell over there.

255
00:21:19.139 --> 00:21:21.415
POOLE: We got a car there now.

256
00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.578
[Tires screeching]

257
00:21:33.982 --> 00:21:35.381
[Dog barking]

258
00:21:49.784 --> 00:21:52.059
Get a couple of shots of that.

259
00:21:54.905 --> 00:21:56.861
POOLE: Fredrick Sykes...

260
00:21:57.065 --> 00:22:00.422
...45. ex-cop. and quite a clotheshorse.

261
00:22:01.706 --> 00:22:04.174
Deputy. you want to look at this?

262
00:22:04.266 --> 00:22:05.335
Yeah.

263
00:22:05.426 --> 00:22:07.463
Kimble's prints. They're all over...

264
00:22:07.547 --> 00:22:09.344
...but mainly on the desk.

265
00:22:09.507 --> 00:22:12.499
He sure had some interest
in these photographs.

266
00:22:12.667 --> 00:22:13.862
SAM: Negatives in there?

267
00:22:13.948 --> 00:22:15.267
SAM: Let me have them.

268
00:22:15.348 --> 00:22:18.704
BIGGS: <i>Camera boy's on his way.</i>
HENRY: We got you.

269
00:22:34.271 --> 00:22:35.829
How're you doing. Mr. Sykes?

270
00:22:35.911 --> 00:22:37.424
SYKES:
Fine. if you tell me what's happening.

271
00:22:37.511 --> 00:22:39.025
BIGGS: We had a problem.

272
00:22:39.112 --> 00:22:42.866
SYKES: My place or the place upstairs?
BIGGS: Your place.

273
00:22:42.952 --> 00:22:44.624
ROSETTl: Step right in. Mr. Sykes.

274
00:22:44.712 --> 00:22:48.103
Everybody knows my name here.
Big happy family. huh?

275
00:22:48.193 --> 00:22:51.424
SYKES: <i>What is this. a trench coat</i>
<i>convention? What the hell is going on?</i>

276
00:22:51.513 --> 00:22:54.472
SYKES: <i>Who are you guys?</i>
<i>What's going on?</i>

277
00:22:57.674 --> 00:22:59.745
You had a break-in. Mr. Sykes.

278
00:23:00.235 --> 00:23:01.953
I sure hope you're a cop.

279
00:23:02.315 --> 00:23:05.308
No. I'm Samuel Gerard.
United States Marshal's Office.

280
00:23:06.156 --> 00:23:10.627
SAM: <i>This morning a fugitive named</i>
<i>Kimble made a phone call from here.</i>

281
00:23:11.116 --> 00:23:12.596
Why would he do that?

282
00:23:13.037 --> 00:23:15.107
I don't know any Richard Kimble.

283
00:23:20.998 --> 00:23:22.750
Okay. I got it.

284
00:23:23.078 --> 00:23:25.354
The doctor who killed his wife. right?

285
00:23:25.679 --> 00:23:29.513
Keep blaming somebody with
a prosthetic limb. Is he coming after me?

286
00:23:29.679 --> 00:23:31.477
Does he have reason to do so?

287
00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:34.154
I have a prosthetic arm! I must've done it!

288
00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:38.033
SYKES: <i>Give me a break.</i>
<i>I went through all this a year ago.</i>

289
00:23:38.121 --> 00:23:40.794
I was questioned here
about the whole thing.

290
00:23:40.881 --> 00:23:45.080
I told them I wasn't in Chicago
on that night. I was on a business trip.

291
00:23:45.162 --> 00:23:46.720
15 people verified it.

292
00:23:46.802 --> 00:23:49.111
What line of business are you in.
Mr. Sykes?

293
00:23:49.202 --> 00:23:50.191
Security.

294
00:23:50.282 --> 00:23:52.751
SAM: <i>Who do you work for?</i>
SYKES: A pharmaceutical company.

295
00:23:52.843 --> 00:23:53.719
Which one?

296
00:23:53.803 --> 00:23:57.877
Devlin MacGregor.
I handle security for all the top executives.

297
00:23:59.084 --> 00:24:02.997
Do you have any idea why Kimble would
be interested in these photographs?

298
00:24:03.925 --> 00:24:04.994
No.

299
00:24:05.685 --> 00:24:07.721
Where were they taken?

300
00:24:07.885 --> 00:24:09.364
Gee. that's a big fish!

301
00:24:09.445 --> 00:24:10.845
SYKES: <i>Cancún. Mexico.</i>

302
00:24:10.926 --> 00:24:13.759
It was a junket the company
paid for some doctors.

303
00:24:13.846 --> 00:24:17.999
SAM: Kimble go with you?
SYKES: You don't see him there. do you?

304
00:24:19.247 --> 00:24:21.807
No. I told you I don't know him.

305
00:24:22.167 --> 00:24:25.080
SYKES: Do you mind if I look around to see
if anything's missing?

306
00:24:25.168 --> 00:24:26.521
No. I don't mind.

307
00:24:32.209 --> 00:24:33.847
How'd you lose that arm?

308
00:24:34.009 --> 00:24:35.601
In the line of duty.

309
00:24:40.730 --> 00:24:42.288
[Birds chirping]

310
00:24:43.251 --> 00:24:44.889
[Sam sighs deeply]

311
00:24:45.371 --> 00:24:47.327
Cosmo. this guy's dirty.

312
00:24:47.731 --> 00:24:49.369
COSMO: Yes. he is.

313
00:24:49.692 --> 00:24:52.968
COSMO: You want our people on him?
SAM: Yes. Build a camp here.

314
00:24:53.052 --> 00:24:55.361
SAM: Henry?
HENRY: I'll take care of it.

315
00:24:55.452 --> 00:24:59.844
Noah? See this picture? I want you
to find out who's the guy next to Sykes.

316
00:24:59.933 --> 00:25:03.290
Find out his name. his age. his weight.
his social security number...

317
00:25:03.374 --> 00:25:06.491
...his location. relatives. pets. everything.

318
00:25:26.177 --> 00:25:30.456
[Whispering] I am so sorry. Doctor.
they said it was an emergency.

319
00:25:31.938 --> 00:25:33.496
Thank you. Excuse me.

320
00:25:42.820 --> 00:25:44.219
[Phone rings]

321
00:25:45.380 --> 00:25:46.699
CHARLES: <i>Mr. Bolton.</i>

322
00:25:46.780 --> 00:25:47.815
Chuck.

323
00:25:47.900 --> 00:25:48.970
CHARLES: <i>Richard.</i>

324
00:25:49.061 --> 00:25:50.255
Yeah. can you talk?

325
00:25:50.341 --> 00:25:54.175
Yes. I'm on a hotel phone.
So how are you? What's going on?

326
00:25:54.982 --> 00:25:58.019
I found him. Chuck.
I found the man who killed Helen.

327
00:25:59.542 --> 00:26:01.579
CHARLES: What?
RICHARD: It was me they were after.

328
00:26:01.663 --> 00:26:02.812
Who are they?

329
00:26:04.063 --> 00:26:06.623
Devlin MacGregor and Lentz.

330
00:26:07.143 --> 00:26:10.022
Lentz was supervising
the protocol for RDU-90.

331
00:26:10.184 --> 00:26:13.620
He knew I found out it was causing liver
damage. It was Lentz.

332
00:26:15.145 --> 00:26:17.739
Richard. Lentz is dead.

333
00:26:19.425 --> 00:26:20.460
What? How?

334
00:26:20.545 --> 00:26:23.777
CHARLES:
<i>He died in a car accident last summer.</i>

335
00:26:27.907 --> 00:26:29.943
Can you prove this about the drug?

336
00:26:30.627 --> 00:26:31.980
Yeah. I think so.

337
00:26:33.187 --> 00:26:34.826
I need your help. Chuck.

338
00:26:35.108 --> 00:26:38.896
Call Bones at the hospital.
Tell him to give me whatever help I need.

339
00:26:39.788 --> 00:26:40.983
I'll call him now.

340
00:26:41.069 --> 00:26:42.502
Okay. Thanks.

341
00:26:49.390 --> 00:26:52.029
MAN: Dr. Nichols...
CHARLES: Hey. how are you?

342
00:26:52.110 --> 00:26:53.429
Dr. Nichols!

343
00:26:53.711 --> 00:26:56.179
SAM: Can we ask you
a few more questions?

344
00:26:56.271 --> 00:26:57.704
Mr. Gerard.

345
00:26:57.871 --> 00:27:00.261
You got a copy of that photograph?

346
00:27:00.552 --> 00:27:01.951
SAM: U.S. Marshal Service.

347
00:27:02.032 --> 00:27:03.260
Excuse us.

348
00:27:06.312 --> 00:27:07.905
This is Fredrick Sykes.

349
00:27:08.073 --> 00:27:11.907
He's a security specialist
at Devlin MacGregor Pharmaceuticals.

350
00:27:12.073 --> 00:27:14.383
Richard Kimble broke into his apartment.

351
00:27:14.474 --> 00:27:15.873
Do you know this man?

352
00:27:15.954 --> 00:27:17.433
No. I don't know him.

353
00:27:18.954 --> 00:27:21.947
You're getting pretty desperate.
aren't you. Mr. Gerard?

354
00:27:22.035 --> 00:27:23.434
Oh. yeah.

355
00:27:24.075 --> 00:27:26.066
I told you. you wouldn't find Richard.

356
00:27:26.156 --> 00:27:28.989
SAM: Has he been to see you?
CHARLES: No.

357
00:27:30.036 --> 00:27:33.234
We've been over this ground before.
haven't we?

358
00:27:33.317 --> 00:27:34.272
Yeah.

359
00:27:35.277 --> 00:27:38.269
CHARLES: So. if you'll excuse me.
SAM: Sure.

360
00:27:39.478 --> 00:27:42.436
SAM: Thanks. Doc.
COSMO: Thank you. Doctor.

361
00:27:43.278 --> 00:27:46.555
Sorry. I want to ask you
one more question about the photograph.

362
00:27:46.639 --> 00:27:49.472
See the guy standing
on the right side of the fish?

363
00:27:49.559 --> 00:27:50.992
Ever see him before?

364
00:27:51.319 --> 00:27:53.038
This guy right here?

365
00:27:53.560 --> 00:27:56.120
I've never seen that person
in my life before.

366
00:27:56.760 --> 00:27:58.079
SAM: Okay.
CHARLES: I'm sorry.

367
00:27:58.160 --> 00:27:59.389
Thank you.

368
00:27:59.481 --> 00:28:02.837
Thank you. Doctor.
Enjoy the rest of the convention.

369
00:28:07.442 --> 00:28:12.119
<i>"Alternatives to Cardio-Non-Invasive</i>
<i>Arterial Plaque-Reducing Therapy.</i>

370
00:28:12.283 --> 00:28:14.513
"Keynote speaker. Charles Nichols."

371
00:28:14.683 --> 00:28:17.197
<i>Bet they line up to hear this one.</i>

372
00:28:26.085 --> 00:28:27.484
[Siren wails]

373
00:28:32.246 --> 00:28:34.521
If you were Richard Kimble...

374
00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:38.442
...why would you hunt for a one-armed
man you say killed your wife...

375
00:28:38.527 --> 00:28:41.883
...break into his house.
call us up and then split?

376
00:28:42.367 --> 00:28:44.198
I should have been a doctor.

377
00:28:44.407 --> 00:28:48.560
NEWMAN: Look at this blow-up. This guy
in the picture with Sykes. On his shirt.

378
00:28:48.648 --> 00:28:49.763
NEWMAN: Chicago Memorial.

379
00:28:49.848 --> 00:28:50.997
I want to go there.

380
00:28:51.089 --> 00:28:52.204
SAM: Go!

381
00:28:52.489 --> 00:28:53.808
BIGGS: Wait.

382
00:28:56.769 --> 00:28:58.488
Devlin MacGregor...

383
00:28:58.610 --> 00:29:02.125
...did 71/2 billion dollars in net sales...

384
00:29:03.090 --> 00:29:04.763
...last year alone.

385
00:29:06.451 --> 00:29:08.362
That company is a monster.

386
00:29:14.372 --> 00:29:15.771
[Phone rings]

387
00:29:16.532 --> 00:29:17.886
Yeah. talk to me.

388
00:29:22.053 --> 00:29:23.406
Absolutely.

389
00:29:24.494 --> 00:29:25.973
RICHARD: <i>It's a liver sample...</i>

390
00:29:26.054 --> 00:29:28.852
<i>... from a patient on the RDU-90 drug study.</i>

391
00:29:28.934 --> 00:29:31.051
RICHARD: <i>21. January 21st?</i>

392
00:29:32.335 --> 00:29:34.087
BONES: The last one!

393
00:29:34.695 --> 00:29:35.923
1-7-4-3-0?

394
00:29:36.135 --> 00:29:38.366
1-7-4-3-0. You got it.

395
00:29:39.736 --> 00:29:43.810
Thanks. Bones. I'll make sure
all this stuff gets back to you.

396
00:29:47.097 --> 00:29:49.486
RICHARD: It's good to see you again.
BONES: Good to see you.

397
00:29:49.577 --> 00:29:53.332
BONES: <i>So whatever happened</i>
<i>to that thing with your wife?</i>

398
00:29:54.858 --> 00:29:56.497
It's not over yet.

399
00:29:57.979 --> 00:30:00.095
[Siren wailing. horn blows]

400
00:30:16.142 --> 00:30:18.053
Hey. Rosetti. What's going on?

401
00:30:18.142 --> 00:30:19.780
How should I know?

402
00:30:32.064 --> 00:30:35.295
I think his name is Alec Lentz.
A pathologist.

403
00:30:36.145 --> 00:30:38.420
I remember because he died last summer.

404
00:30:46.866 --> 00:30:48.778
Oh. my God. Richard!

405
00:30:49.267 --> 00:30:51.178
What are you doing here?

406
00:30:51.507 --> 00:30:52.781
Hi. Kath.

407
00:31:07.669 --> 00:31:09.388
KATHY: <i>Have a look.</i>

408
00:31:11.110 --> 00:31:13.499
KATHY: <i>What do you think?</i>
RICHARD: Cold normal.

409
00:31:13.590 --> 00:31:15.741
Clearly not the same tissue.

410
00:31:15.911 --> 00:31:19.426
And not only did they all
come from healthy livers...

411
00:31:19.911 --> 00:31:22.107
...they all came from the same liver.

412
00:31:23.912 --> 00:31:25.504
Kath. you beauty.

413
00:31:30.633 --> 00:31:31.588
[Bones humming to himself]

414
00:31:31.673 --> 00:31:33.311
NEWMAN: <i>Excuse me.</i>

415
00:31:33.593 --> 00:31:35.471
NEWMAN: Mr. Roosevelt?

416
00:31:36.234 --> 00:31:39.670
I am Deputy Biggs. this is
Deputy Newman. We're U.S. Marshals.

417
00:31:39.754 --> 00:31:43.191
Need some information about a Dr. Lentz
who was on staff here.

418
00:31:43.355 --> 00:31:47.747
I want to know if he knew or had
had any contact with a Dr. Richard Kimble?

419
00:31:48.076 --> 00:31:49.907
I haven't seen Dr. Kimble.

420
00:31:51.036 --> 00:31:52.389
I didn't ask that.

421
00:31:53.436 --> 00:31:54.870
I wouldn't know.

422
00:31:55.197 --> 00:31:58.872
If you'll excuse me.
I have prior obligations to attend to.

423
00:32:01.758 --> 00:32:04.318
NEWMAN: <i>I think you're lying to us.</i>

424
00:32:04.798 --> 00:32:07.154
You think Lentz is the bad guy?

425
00:32:07.759 --> 00:32:09.192
Yeah. why not?

426
00:32:10.719 --> 00:32:14.156
He was one of the original
patent boys in RDU-90.

427
00:32:15.440 --> 00:32:17.635
I was sending in my tissue samples...

428
00:32:18.160 --> 00:32:21.836
...he was replacing them with healthy
samples. issuing the path reports...

429
00:32:21.921 --> 00:32:23.752
...shit-canning my stuff. Easy.

430
00:32:23.841 --> 00:32:25.274
KATHY: Wait a minute.

431
00:32:25.361 --> 00:32:27.671
Lentz died August 21st.

432
00:32:29.682 --> 00:32:33.915
Half the samples he approved
were signed the day he died.

433
00:32:35.203 --> 00:32:36.431
You're kidding.

434
00:32:38.243 --> 00:32:40.883
Someone else must have been
manipulating this.

435
00:32:41.524 --> 00:32:42.957
Someone with access.

436
00:32:54.166 --> 00:32:55.360
Thanks. Kath.

437
00:32:55.766 --> 00:32:57.165
Where're you going?

438
00:32:58.486 --> 00:32:59.840
To see a friend.

439
00:33:04.967 --> 00:33:06.799
This is giving me a headache.

440
00:33:07.128 --> 00:33:10.803
That's surprising. Where did
Roosevelt say Kimble was going?

441
00:33:10.968 --> 00:33:13.039
He says he doesn't know.

442
00:33:13.449 --> 00:33:15.280
SAM: Do you believe him?
NEWMAN: <i>Yes. I do.</i>

443
00:33:15.369 --> 00:33:18.008
NEWMAN: <i>He says he was here to pick up</i>
<i>some tissue samples...</i>

444
00:33:18.089 --> 00:33:19.523
<i>... for a drug study.</i>

445
00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.169
But listen. get this.

446
00:33:21.290 --> 00:33:24.248
The release was approved
by Dr. Charles Nichols.

447
00:33:24.970 --> 00:33:27.360
NEWMAN: <i>Nichols also knew Lentz.</i>

448
00:33:28.331 --> 00:33:29.764
NEWMAN: <i>He was Lentz's boss.</i>

449
00:33:29.851 --> 00:33:31.364
He was covering for Kimble.

450
00:33:31.451 --> 00:33:33.283
Send the C.P.D. Over there right now.

451
00:33:33.372 --> 00:33:37.604
We're going to send a bunch of cops.
Make sure they turn that place inside out.

452
00:33:37.692 --> 00:33:41.208
Don't let them give you shit
about your ponytail either. Well done.

453
00:33:41.293 --> 00:33:42.646
My pleasure. Sam.

454
00:33:45.374 --> 00:33:47.285
Henry. Dr. Nichols lied to me.

455
00:33:47.374 --> 00:33:49.888
SAM: Go find him.
HENRY: I'm on it.

456
00:33:53.695 --> 00:33:55.094
[Train roars]

457
00:33:56.815 --> 00:33:58.295
SYKES: <i>He's gone by now.</i>

458
00:33:58.376 --> 00:34:01.846
I looked every place you told me
to look and I didn't see him.

459
00:34:01.936 --> 00:34:03.130
I'm telling you.

460
00:34:03.216 --> 00:34:06.254
If he was in the hospital.
I would have found him.

461
00:34:06.337 --> 00:34:08.168
So what do you want me to do?

462
00:34:09.137 --> 00:34:10.889
Hold on. Wait a minute.

463
00:34:11.138 --> 00:34:13.368
I marked him. I got him now.

464
00:34:41.302 --> 00:34:43.452
Dr. Alexander Lentz.

465
00:34:43.863 --> 00:34:46.900
"A noted pathologist
at Chicago Memorial Hospital...

466
00:34:47.063 --> 00:34:50.579
<i>"...was walking to his daily tennis match</i>
<i>when an unidentified vehicle...</i>

467
00:34:50.664 --> 00:34:52.097
"...slammed his body...

468
00:34:52.184 --> 00:34:55.859
"...into the barriers that separate
the Drive from Lake Michigan."

469
00:34:56.144 --> 00:34:57.100
Yuck!

470
00:34:58.385 --> 00:35:00.376
Sam. you're not going to believe this.

471
00:35:00.465 --> 00:35:04.095
STEVENS: Sykes' records for the past
two years show no calls to Kimble.

472
00:35:04.186 --> 00:35:05.301
It was a thought.

473
00:35:05.386 --> 00:35:08.981
But when I cross-checked
Kimble's phone records. one came up.

474
00:35:09.066 --> 00:35:10.625
Kimble called Sykes...

475
00:35:12.587 --> 00:35:14.020
Get Sykes in here now.

476
00:35:14.107 --> 00:35:15.779
STEVENS: <i>... on the night of the murder...</i>

477
00:35:15.867 --> 00:35:17.221
...7:30 P. M...

478
00:35:17.388 --> 00:35:18.821
<i>... from his car phone.</i>

479
00:35:18.908 --> 00:35:21.297
Do you have the arrest report on Kimble?

480
00:35:26.989 --> 00:35:29.550
SAM: 7:30 P.M.
STEVENS: 19:30 hours.

481
00:35:30.510 --> 00:35:32.740
They just went in. Sykes is gone.

482
00:35:32.910 --> 00:35:35.060
POOLE: <i>He's nowhere to be found.</i>

483
00:35:35.150 --> 00:35:36.379
He's gone.

484
00:35:37.591 --> 00:35:38.990
[Train roars]

485
00:36:38.280 --> 00:36:42.911
Possible sighting of Richard Kimble
on northbound El coming into Van Buren.

486
00:36:49.002 --> 00:36:50.879
Move to the door. Doc.

487
00:36:58.003 --> 00:37:00.563
INTERCOM: <i>Next stop. Balbo station.</i>

488
00:37:01.884 --> 00:37:03.442
This is my stop.

489
00:37:04.844 --> 00:37:06.596
This is my stop too.

490
00:37:07.485 --> 00:37:08.554
Kimble!

491
00:37:08.645 --> 00:37:10.203
[Loud gun blast]

492
00:37:13.365 --> 00:37:15.402
[Metal wheels screeching]

493
00:37:19.446 --> 00:37:21.005
[Sykes grunting]

494
00:37:29.208 --> 00:37:31.164
[Sykes groans and yells]

495
00:38:04.253 --> 00:38:05.766
You missed your stop.

496
00:38:06.494 --> 00:38:07.768
[Loud thud]

497
00:38:12.494 --> 00:38:14.087
[Violent shattering]

498
00:38:26.257 --> 00:38:27.485
Sam. Sam.

499
00:38:27.857 --> 00:38:31.406
A transit cop spotted Kimble on the EI.
he is heading toward Balbo.

500
00:38:31.497 --> 00:38:33.534
The C.P.D. Is on the way.

501
00:38:33.858 --> 00:38:35.450
[Chopper humming]

502
00:38:58.302 --> 00:38:59.860
[Sirens wailing]

503
00:39:07.383 --> 00:39:12.094
C. B: <i>Attention all units. Transit police</i>
<i>report officer down at Balbo Station.</i>

504
00:39:12.184 --> 00:39:14.857
C. B: <i>Kimble is suspect.</i>
<i>Repeat officer down.</i>

505
00:39:14.944 --> 00:39:16.423
What'd he do. shoot a cop?

506
00:39:16.504 --> 00:39:18.655
COSMO: Chicago P.D. Will eat him alive.

507
00:39:25.506 --> 00:39:30.341
HOST: It is a joy and a privilege...
to introduce tonight's keynote speaker.

508
00:39:39.548 --> 00:39:41.300
For the past four years...

509
00:39:41.468 --> 00:39:44.666
...he has served as
the A. Jude Robinson Fellow...

510
00:39:44.829 --> 00:39:47.866
...and Administrative Chief of Pathology...

511
00:39:48.029 --> 00:39:50.338
<i>... at Chicago Memorial Hospital.</i>

512
00:39:54.790 --> 00:39:57.066
Where are the emergency exits?

513
00:39:58.031 --> 00:40:02.582
C. B: <i>Suspect seen entering</i>
<i>Hilton Tower Mall. lower level. Repeat...</i>

514
00:40:02.671 --> 00:40:03.787
COSMO: <i>You don't think</i>...

515
00:40:03.872 --> 00:40:05.828
I know where he's going.

516
00:40:07.232 --> 00:40:09.871
COSMO: <i>Biggs. Newman. where are you?</i>

517
00:40:10.393 --> 00:40:13.305
He was appointed
to the Board of Directors...

518
00:40:13.393 --> 00:40:15.702
...of Devlin MacGregor Pharmaceuticals.

519
00:40:15.913 --> 00:40:18.109
<i>You all please give a warm welcome...</i>

520
00:40:18.314 --> 00:40:20.384
...to Dr. Charles Nichols.

521
00:40:21.674 --> 00:40:22.902
[Applause]

522
00:40:26.635 --> 00:40:29.149
Thank you very much.
ladies and gentlemen...

523
00:40:29.235 --> 00:40:31.147
...my friends and colleagues.

524
00:40:31.596 --> 00:40:34.668
CHARLES: <i>It's great you're all here tonight.</i>

525
00:40:36.717 --> 00:40:38.947
[Sirens blare. tires screech]

526
00:40:46.038 --> 00:40:49.509
NEWMAN: C.P.D. Reported an officer down
and a guy with two guns...

527
00:40:49.599 --> 00:40:51.590
SAM: Kimble do it?
BIGGS: Conflicting reports.

528
00:40:51.679 --> 00:40:53.510
He entered the hotel from the subway.

529
00:40:53.599 --> 00:40:55.317
SAM: That's my man!
ROSETTl: Not anymore.

530
00:40:55.399 --> 00:40:57.550
He's going down.
You can help by staying out.

531
00:40:57.640 --> 00:40:58.914
Arrest us!

532
00:40:59.080 --> 00:41:02.072
SAM: <i>Lock it up! Start at the lower level.</i>

533
00:41:03.881 --> 00:41:06.395
<i>All units report when lower level is secure.</i>

534
00:41:08.601 --> 00:41:11.241
<i>All units. secure all lower level exits.</i>

535
00:41:12.042 --> 00:41:17.117
Noah. go and find the hotel security office.
Stay in touch with me on the radio.

536
00:41:18.603 --> 00:41:20.161
CHARLES: <i>Now. a new drug...</i>

537
00:41:20.243 --> 00:41:24.283
<i>... on the cusp of approval</i>
<i>by the Food and Drug Administration...</i>

538
00:41:24.364 --> 00:41:28.152
<i>... is poised to change</i>
<i>these old methods forever.</i>

539
00:41:29.045 --> 00:41:31.275
Deputy Newman. U.S. Marshal's Service.

540
00:41:32.605 --> 00:41:34.038
Sam. I'm in.

541
00:41:37.646 --> 00:41:41.161
<i>... through the normal metabolic pathways</i>
<i>in the liver.</i>

542
00:41:42.287 --> 00:41:44.357
<i>The drug's name is...</i>

543
00:41:44.527 --> 00:41:45.846
...Provasic.

544
00:41:47.287 --> 00:41:49.438
CHARLES: <i>As I will show you tonight...</i>

545
00:41:49.528 --> 00:41:52.281
...Provasic is remarkably effective...

546
00:41:52.408 --> 00:41:55.446
<i>... and has no side effects whatsoever.</i>

547
00:41:55.729 --> 00:41:58.289
It is also noteworthy that this drug...

548
00:42:03.330 --> 00:42:05.446
...that this drug was developed...

549
00:42:05.610 --> 00:42:08.808
<i>... in cooperation. not competition</i>
<i>with Chicago Memorial Hospital...</i>

550
00:42:08.891 --> 00:42:10.643
<i>... in what we hope will be...</i>

551
00:42:10.731 --> 00:42:13.450
...the model for a continued dishonest...

552
00:42:14.172 --> 00:42:15.810
...excuse me. honest...

553
00:42:19.212 --> 00:42:20.565
<i>... open joint venture...</i>

554
00:42:20.652 --> 00:42:23.042
...between academic medicine...

555
00:42:23.213 --> 00:42:25.329
<i>... and the pharmaceutical industry...</i>

556
00:42:25.413 --> 00:42:26.641
<i>Richard!</i>

557
00:42:28.014 --> 00:42:31.290
I'm sorry. I'm in the middle of this speech.

558
00:42:31.774 --> 00:42:33.605
You almost got away with it.

559
00:42:35.975 --> 00:42:37.454
I know all about it.

560
00:42:39.215 --> 00:42:40.490
I can prove it.

561
00:42:41.936 --> 00:42:45.690
Ladies and gentlemen. my friend.
Richard Kimble. doesn't feel well...

562
00:42:45.936 --> 00:42:47.609
CHARLES: <i>... obviously...</i>

563
00:42:47.697 --> 00:42:51.053
<i>... so if you just go on</i>
<i>with your dessert and coffee...</i>

564
00:42:51.137 --> 00:42:54.494
Richard. would you step aside
and let's talk.

565
00:42:56.178 --> 00:42:58.646
So I'll be back in just a second.

566
00:43:02.859 --> 00:43:05.134
You changed the samples. didn't you?

567
00:43:06.820 --> 00:43:09.095
You switched the samples...

568
00:43:09.220 --> 00:43:10.812
...after Lentz died.

569
00:43:12.540 --> 00:43:14.816
HOST: <i>Let's stay calm. people.</i>

570
00:43:16.301 --> 00:43:19.533
After Lentz died. you were
the only one who had access.

571
00:43:20.662 --> 00:43:22.653
You switched the samples...

572
00:43:23.142 --> 00:43:25.292
...and the pathology reports.

573
00:43:25.462 --> 00:43:26.896
You killed Lentz too?

574
00:43:26.983 --> 00:43:28.302
<i>Call Security.</i>

575
00:43:28.423 --> 00:43:29.981
RICHARD: Did you?

576
00:43:30.263 --> 00:43:32.458
He falsified his research...

577
00:43:34.064 --> 00:43:36.339
...so RDU-90 could be...

578
00:43:36.504 --> 00:43:37.857
...approved and...

579
00:43:38.024 --> 00:43:41.062
...Devlin MacGregor
could give you Provasic.

580
00:43:43.185 --> 00:43:44.584
HOST: <i>All right. it's all over. folks.</i>

581
00:43:44.665 --> 00:43:46.224
Let's just stay calm.

582
00:43:52.667 --> 00:43:54.419
[Propellers pelting]

583
00:44:00.908 --> 00:44:01.943
[Loud crash]

584
00:44:02.028 --> 00:44:05.624
You never give up. Richard. do you?
You never give up!

585
00:44:18.831 --> 00:44:20.059
[Groaning]

586
00:44:27.152 --> 00:44:28.301
Why Helen?

587
00:44:31.072 --> 00:44:32.108
SECURITY GUARD: Glad you're here.

588
00:44:32.193 --> 00:44:33.626
Which way'd they go?

589
00:44:33.713 --> 00:44:35.704
GUARD: Toward the Presidential Suite.
SAM: Where's that?

590
00:44:35.793 --> 00:44:37.146
GUARD: Southeast corner.

591
00:44:37.233 --> 00:44:38.553
SAM: How many exits
are there in this room?

592
00:44:38.634 --> 00:44:42.388
We got a total of four:
Two on the east. two on the west.

593
00:44:43.074 --> 00:44:44.827
NEWMAN: Kimble's on the roof!

594
00:44:44.915 --> 00:44:46.428
Cosmo. that way.

595
00:44:58.637 --> 00:45:00.912
PILOT ON O VERHEAD RADIO:
<i>Stop! Stay where you are!</i>

596
00:45:00.997 --> 00:45:03.113
<i>This is the Chicago police!</i>

597
00:45:03.397 --> 00:45:05.389
<i>Put your hands in the air!</i>

598
00:45:05.478 --> 00:45:07.833
<i>The building is totally secure.</i>

599
00:45:07.958 --> 00:45:09.835
<i>I repeat. do not move!</i>

600
00:45:11.159 --> 00:45:13.229
<i>Put your hands in the air!</i>

601
00:45:14.399 --> 00:45:16.629
<i>I repeat. stay where you are!</i>

602
00:45:38.523 --> 00:45:39.717
Talk to me.

603
00:45:39.883 --> 00:45:42.443
They're headed to the north end
of the roof.

604
00:45:42.563 --> 00:45:44.043
SAM: Newman!

605
00:45:44.644 --> 00:45:47.033
Get that helicopter out of here!

606
00:45:50.285 --> 00:45:52.355
As soon as you get a clean shot...

607
00:45:52.445 --> 00:45:54.037
...you take him out.

608
00:46:03.887 --> 00:46:05.798
[Multiple rifle blasts]

609
00:46:11.528 --> 00:46:13.484
Newman. get rid of the helicopter!

610
00:46:13.568 --> 00:46:15.878
NEWMAN: <i>Why?</i>
SAM: Because I don't want to get shot!

611
00:46:15.969 --> 00:46:19.803
C.P.D.. there's a U.S. Marshal
out on the roof. Hold your fire!

612
00:46:20.049 --> 00:46:22.439
NEWMAN: <i>Call off the helicopter!</i>

613
00:46:32.531 --> 00:46:33.850
[Painful groan]

614
00:46:41.732 --> 00:46:43.325
[Violent shattering]

615
00:46:54.854 --> 00:46:56.334
[Loud crashing]

616
00:47:02.376 --> 00:47:03.968
[Machine buzzing]

617
00:47:07.896 --> 00:47:09.171
Don't shoot.

618
00:47:12.377 --> 00:47:14.208
COSMO: This guy ever quit?

619
00:47:14.297 --> 00:47:16.858
Find out where that elevator stops.

620
00:47:17.658 --> 00:47:19.933
Newman. Northwest elevator!
Where does it stop?

621
00:47:20.018 --> 00:47:22.214
Where did they go? Where did they go?

622
00:47:51.503 --> 00:47:53.414
GUARD: Stopped on the 5th floor.
NEWMAN: They're on the 5th floor.

623
00:47:53.503 --> 00:47:57.258
NEWMAN: What's on the 5th floor?
GUARD: It's the laundry.

624
00:47:57.344 --> 00:47:59.983
NEWMAN: <i>They stopped at the laundry.</i>

625
00:48:06.305 --> 00:48:08.024
[Breathing heavily]

626
00:48:29.669 --> 00:48:31.148
[Steam hissing]

627
00:48:41.431 --> 00:48:44.662
COSMO: We're on the 5th floor.
What's your 20?

628
00:48:45.351 --> 00:48:46.785
BIGGS: It's right behind you.

629
00:48:46.872 --> 00:48:48.942
BIGGS: What the hell is going on here?

630
00:48:49.032 --> 00:48:52.149
You got to keep the C.P.D. Out.
They're much too hot to suit me.

631
00:48:52.232 --> 00:48:54.303
I want you to get rid of all these people.

632
00:48:54.393 --> 00:48:55.746
POOLE: <i>Okay. people. stay calm.</i>

633
00:48:55.833 --> 00:48:57.869
SAM: Cosmo. come with me.

634
00:49:38.960 --> 00:49:40.439
[Steam hissing]

635
00:50:15.445 --> 00:50:17.402
SAM: <i>Dr. Richard Kimble!</i>

636
00:50:18.646 --> 00:50:20.762
There's no way out of here. Richard!

637
00:50:22.086 --> 00:50:24.920
SAM: <i>The entire building is locked down!</i>

638
00:50:27.207 --> 00:50:29.277
Give it up. you don't have any time!

639
00:50:29.367 --> 00:50:33.122
SAM: <i>Chicago Police Department thinks</i>
<i>you're a cop killer!</i>

640
00:50:33.208 --> 00:50:35.722
SAM: <i>They will shoot you on sight!</i>

641
00:50:39.209 --> 00:50:41.882
SAM: <i>Richard. I know you're innocent!</i>

642
00:50:42.569 --> 00:50:44.765
I know about Fredrick Sykes!

643
00:50:47.450 --> 00:50:50.170
SAM: <i>I know about Dr. Charles Nichols!</i>

644
00:50:52.011 --> 00:50:55.287
SAM: <i>Richard. he borrowed your car</i>
<i>the night of your wife's murder!</i>

645
00:50:55.371 --> 00:50:57.044
SAM: <i>He had the keys!</i>

646
00:50:57.132 --> 00:50:59.407
SAM: <i>No forced entry. Richard.</i>

647
00:51:00.252 --> 00:51:03.484
SAM: <i>He telephoned Sykes</i>
<i>from your car. Richard!</i>

648
00:51:10.334 --> 00:51:12.370
SAM: <i>Richard. give it up!</i>

649
00:51:14.254 --> 00:51:17.884
SAM: <i>I'm either lying to you</i>
<i>or I'm going to shoot you!</i>

650
00:51:18.255 --> 00:51:20.166
SAM: <i>What do you think?</i>

651
00:51:38.258 --> 00:51:41.056
Give it up! It's time to stop running!

652
00:51:43.539 --> 00:51:44.813
[Loud yelp]

653
00:51:45.899 --> 00:51:47.127
[Groaning]

654
00:51:51.100 --> 00:51:53.295
[Buzzer ringing in distance]

655
00:52:03.382 --> 00:52:04.861
[Steam hissing]

656
00:52:20.464 --> 00:52:22.183
They killed my wife.

657
00:52:22.985 --> 00:52:24.384
I know it. Richard.

658
00:52:25.865 --> 00:52:27.014
I know it.

659
00:52:28.946 --> 00:52:30.379
But. it's over now.

660
00:52:33.066 --> 00:52:35.058
[Sighing] You know. I'm glad.

661
00:52:35.147 --> 00:52:36.739
I need the rest.

662
00:52:46.508 --> 00:52:48.101
[Chaotic yelling]

663
00:52:50.829 --> 00:52:52.740
REPORTER 1: Who killed Kimble's wife?

664
00:52:52.829 --> 00:52:54.741
KELLY: <i>Kimble was convicted of it.</i>

665
00:52:54.830 --> 00:52:57.549
REPORTER 2:
You've got a one-armed man in custody.

666
00:52:57.630 --> 00:52:59.586
REPORTER 2: Is that the guy?
KELLY: <i>I have no idea.</i>

667
00:52:59.670 --> 00:53:01.389
REPORTER 1:
How many one-armed men are there?

668
00:53:01.471 --> 00:53:03.109
KELLY: There're a lot of them.

669
00:53:03.191 --> 00:53:06.149
REPORTER 1:
<i>Could you have made a mistake?</i>

670
00:53:08.632 --> 00:53:10.384
[Flashbulb popping]

671
00:53:12.592 --> 00:53:15.312
ROSETTl: <i>You got a deadline.</i>
<i>play the weather again.</i>

672
00:53:15.393 --> 00:53:19.944
COSMO: Tell Samuel Gerard I'm going
home now. I'm taking my vacation.

673
00:53:22.714 --> 00:53:25.626
POOLE: <i>Clear this area. Everybody clear.</i>

674
00:53:30.555 --> 00:53:32.147
[Chaotic yelling]

675
00:53:41.917 --> 00:53:43.828
BIGGS: Watch your head.

676
00:53:53.919 --> 00:53:56.035
Poole. where is that thing?

677
00:53:56.279 --> 00:53:58.634
Let me see those hands. Doctor.

678
00:54:15.882 --> 00:54:17.474
I thought you didn't care.

679
00:54:17.562 --> 00:54:18.677
I don't.

680
00:54:19.723 --> 00:54:20.997
[Chuckling]

681
00:54:21.643 --> 00:54:23.679
Don't tell anybody. okay?

682
00:54:28.684 --> 00:54:30.481
Subtitles conformed by SOFTITLER
